{"tool_name":"cpss","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"cpss","home":"http://114.214.166.79/cpss2.0/","summary":"Computational platform update for the analysis of small RNA sequencing data.","addition_date":"2018-06-05T12:33:36Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:38:24.202847Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"version":["2.0"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:cpss","credit":[{"email":"qshi@ustc.edu.cn","name":"Qinghua Shi","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"zyuanwei@ustc.edu.cn","name":"Yuanwei Zhang","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://114.214.166.79/cpss2.0/help.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"RNA-Seq analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3680"}]}],"name":"CPSS","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"d.gabrielaitis","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btx066","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary Next-generation sequencing has been widely applied to understand the complexity of non-coding RNAs (ncRNAs) in the last decades. Here, we present CPSS 2.0, an updated version of CPSS 1.0 for small RNA sequencing data analysis, with the following improvements: (i) a substantial increase of supported species from 10 to 48; (ii) improved strategies applied to detect ncRNAs; (iii) more ncRNAs can be detected and profiled, such as lncRNA and circRNA; (iv) identification of differentially expressed ncRNAs among multiple samples; (v) enhanced visualization interface containing graphs and charts in detailed analysis results. The new version of CPSS is an efficient bioinformatics tool for users in non-coding RNA research.","authors":[{"name":"Ban R."},{"name":"Gao J."},{"name":"Jiang X."},{"name":"Shi Q."},{"name":"Wan C."},{"name":"Zang Q."},{"name":"Zhang H."},{"name":"Zhang Y."}],"citationCount":30,"date":"2017-10-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"